mode: "100644"
text: "# Platform Transforms — one atom, native everywhere\n\nHow the *same* core idea becomes each platform's native post. These are transform recipes: feed\nin the atom, get out a version built for that platform. Each changes the hook, format, length,\nmechanics, and register — never just the hashtags.\n\n> For full caption mechanics see `caption-writer/references/platforms.md`; for hook craft per\n> format see `hook-writer/references/formats.md`. This reference is the *transform* layer that\n> sits on top of both. Re-verify platform specs periodically.\n\n---\n\n## → Instagram\n\n- **Native forms:** Reel (video), carousel (visual teaching), single image.\n- **Pick by atom:** a *moment/story* → Reel; a *how-to/list* → carousel; a *single point* →\n  image.\n- **Hook:** visual + on-screen text; caption first line within ~125 chars.\n- **Mechanics:** link in bio; a few relevant hashtags. Register: warm.\n- **CTA:** save / send / follow.\n\n## → TikTok\n\n- **Native form:** short video, 9:16, sound-on, trend/sound-aware.\n- **Transform:** make it faster and looser than the Reel; lead with the hook in frame one;\n  keyword the caption for search.\n- **Register:** casual, native, less polished. (Hand to `tiktok-script` for trend-led ideas.)\n- **CTA:** comment / follow.\n\n## → LinkedIn\n\n- **Native form:** text post (or a document/PDF carousel).\n- **Transform:** expand the atom into a short, whitespace-heavy post; lead with the hook line\n  (~140-char cutoff); more authority/insight register.\n- **Mechanics:** link in comments (not body); 3–5 hashtags. Longer is fine if it earns the read.\n- **CTA:** a genuine question (comments) or a soft point.\n\n## → X / Twitter\n\n- **Native form:** a single punchy post, or a thread for multi-atom ideas.\n- **Transform:** strip to the sharpest line; lead with the point; cut everything else.\n- **Mechanics:** 0–2 hashtags; conversational. (Hand multi-atom ideas to `thread-writer`.)\n- **CTA:** reply / repost, or none — a strong last line earns engagement.\n\n## → Threads\n\n- **Native form:** short, conversational post or light thread.\n- **Transform:** reactive, opinion-forward, lower-polish than LinkedIn; one topic tag.\n- **CTA:** invite replies.\n\n## → Bluesky\n\n- **Native form:** short text post; links are clickable and welcome (no link penalty culture).\n- **Transform:** like X but warmer/less combative; skeet-length punchy take; hashtags barely used.\n- **CTA:** reply / repost.\n\n## → Facebook\n\n- **Native form:** text + image/video post; group-friendly, conversational.\n- **Transform:** slightly longer and more personal than X; lead with a relatable line; minimal\n  hashtags; links fine in the post.\n- **CTA:** comment / share.\n\n## → YouTube Shorts\n\n- **Native form:** short vertical video.\n- **Transform:** like the Reel, but the first line doubles as a **searchable** title; the\n  lean-in audience tolerates a slightly stronger payoff.\n- **CTA:** subscribe / watch the long version.\n\n## → Pinterest\n\n- **Native form:** a pin — image (or video) + **destination link** + keyword-rich description.\n- **Transform:** make it evergreen and **searchable** (keywords, not hashtags); the visual must\n  stand alone; the link is the point (real traffic driver).\n- **CTA:** save / visit the link.\n\n---\n\n## The transform table (quick reference)\n\n| Platform | Native form | Length | Hook | Links | Register |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Instagram | Reel / carousel / image | short–med | visual + text | bio | warm |\n| TikTok | short video | short | frame-one | bio | casual |\n| LinkedIn | text post / doc | med–long | line + whitespace | comments | authority |\n| X | post / thread | short | the point | inline | conversational |\n| Threads | post / light thread | short | the take | inline | casual |\n| Bluesky | short post | short | the take | inline | casual-warm |\n| Facebook | text + media post | short–med | relatable line | inline | personal |\n| YT Shorts | short video | short | searchable line | description | clear |\n| Pinterest | pin + link | short | keyword | clickable | descriptive |\n\nSame atom, nine different builds. If your versions don't differ across these columns, you\nhaven't repurposed — you've relocated.\n"
